# Result table ordering

- Every pagetable or row-based data display must appear before every chart
  that plots individual points.
- Pagetables include the session summary, recent placements, a loss's or
  trial game's "this game" stats, time and day-category rankings such as
  "on weekends", board-shape rankings, streak, near-streak, and
  near-near-streak.
- Point charts include the your-perf property charts, the board-trait
  property charts, and the raw relationship scatterplots.
- Preserve this sequence in both DOM and visual order:
  one table collection (session summary, recent placements, after a loss
  "this game", other rank tables, then all streak variants) → This board
  tables → your-perf charts →
  board-trait charts → relationship charts.
- "Live perf charts" (titled "during this game, second by second" until
  2026-10-20) is not in this sequence: it leads the
  game data column beside the board, above game data (creator decision
  2026-10-15).
- Motion stats is not in this sequence either: one open/close section at
  the page foot, after every result section (creator decision 2026-10-20,
  when the left stats panel was removed).
- The upper tables share one continuous wrapping list without Rankings or
  Streaks section headings. Retain individual table labels such as lifetime
  and near-streak, which identify their data.
- The session summary and recent placements sit left and right of the board
  where each fits (creator decision 2026-10-07). They stay first in the table
  collection's DOM order, not a section of their own. Below the board they
  float as one left column, the summary on top, with nothing above or left
  of it.
- After a loss, the "this game" stats table follows them in DOM order
  (creator decision 2026-10-26: "flowing up as possible"). It takes a side
  of the board neither holds, the left first, where it fits; below the board
  it leads the first row beside their column where it fits there, and
  otherwise floats at the left where that row would have put it.
- Never extract the time-period summary or streaks into a separate section.
- Responsive wrapping must stay within each semantic section and must not
  interleave a pagetable with point charts.
